=== parameters ===
reuse panel 200x750; true factor + nuisance raw_factor2 (noise loading)
look-ahead: shift(1) weights; lagged impact vol; factor[t] → fwd from t+1
cost model shared with P2/P3/P4-01: 10 bps one-way + √impact

=== neutralization before / after ===
true_factor RankIC mean before_neut=0.0845 after=0.1105
nuisance_factor RankIC mean after_neut=0.0029 (should be ~0)
recovery corr after_neut=0.9726

=== single vs equal-weight multi-factor ===
true_only                gross_SR=4.465 net_SR=3.734 turn=0.9349 NAV=34.418 IC=0.1105
nuisance_only            gross_SR=0.873 net_SR=-7.112 turn=1.5619 NAV=0.340 IC=0.0029
ew_true_plus_nuisance    gross_SR=4.509 net_SR=3.093 turn=1.3169 NAV=8.481 IC=0.0810
teach: blending a null nuisance factor dilutes IC and net SR — combining ≠ free lunch

=== turnover–cost table (rebalance cadence) ===
hold= 1d mean_turn=0.9349 net_SR=3.734 NAV=34.418
hold= 5d mean_turn=0.1919 net_SR=4.380 NAV=63.965
hold=10d mean_turn=0.0943 net_SR=4.440 NAV=68.570
hold=20d mean_turn=0.0509 net_SR=4.474 NAV=73.174
teach: lower turnover cuts cost drag; expected-value tradeoff vs signal freshness

=== crowding foil ===
long_leg_HHI_mean=0.02500 rank_AC1=0.8666
teach: high AC + concentrated books → crowding risk if many funds hold the same names
